&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;grid-module__AMTIxG__block border-r-background-200 relative [&amp;amp;_b]:font-medium&quot; data-grid-cell=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, you’ll own a book of named enterprise accounts in Australia and New Zealand and win net-new business at some of the region’s most digitally ambitious companies. You’ll build executive relationships from scratch, then expand platform adoption as Vercel becomes part of each customer’s web and AI roadmap. Success looks like net-new revenue and platform expansion across your named accounts, with hyperscaler, systems integrator, and agency partners in every account plan. This is a hybrid role with 3 in-office days per week in Sydney.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run multi-year account plans for named enterprise accounts, with hyperscaler, systems integrator, and agency partners involved from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win net-new revenue through outbound prospecting, rigorous discovery, and multi-threaded deals across engineering, product, procurement, legal, and the C-suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frame Vercel’s value for executives around developer velocity, infrastructure consolidation, and AI transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate complex commercial agreements and position Vercel as a long-term infrastructure partner in your accounts’ web and AI roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Solutions Engineers and your Partner Manager to bring Vercel into target accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of enterprise SaaS experience closing six and seven-figure deals in major or strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closed deals through co-sell or partner-influenced motions with a hyperscaler, systems integrator, or independent software vendor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Held technical conversations with CTOs and senior engineering leaders, and total cost of ownership conversations with CFOs, without relying on a solutions engineer to carry them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built multi-year account plans for complex accounts, including executive relationships from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Used MEDDPICC to run deals and kept forecasts and CRM records current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience in web development, developer tooling, web infrastructure, cloud platforms, or AI/ML&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have existing relationships at AWS, GCP, or Azure, or at systems integrators and software vendors active in Australia and New Zealand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have sold into media, retail, financial services, or digital-native companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
